{
  "assessment": "The change introduces a slug normalizer that correctly lowercases, sanitizes, and enforces the hard 20-character catalogue width limit. However, it completely omits collision resolution logic. Since the task explicitly warns that truncated slugs collide and cause overwrites, the `assign` function must disambiguate identical prefixes before returning them. Without this logic, any set of similarly titled articles will produce duplicate slugs, directly causing the file overwrite behavior described in the prompt.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "actual": "Both articles receive the identical truncated slug 'how-to-build-a-resil', guaranteeing downstream file collisions and newsletter link mismatches.",
      "at": "pubslug/slugs.py, assign function",
      "call": "python -c \"from pubslug.slugs import assign; print(assign([{'id': 'a1', 'title': 'How to build a resilient ingest pipeline'}, {'id': 'a2', 'title': 'How to build a resilient queue consumer'}]))\"",
      "defect": "Missing collision disambiguation in slug assignment",
      "expected": "A list of dictionaries where each article has a unique slug, with duplicate prefixes resolved via suffixes or alternative routing as defined by docs/slugs.md."
    }
  ]
}
